            <ArticleTitle>Gastric Calcifying Fibrous Tumor Manifesting as a Subepithelial Tumor.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11605-017-3639-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A gastric subepithelial tumor is a common finding during upper gastric endoscopy. The differential diagnosis of such lesions is broad, and sometimes a rare disease can be diagnosed. A calcifying fibrous tumor (CFT) is a rare, benign mesenchymal tumor that usually affects children and young adults. To our knowledge, a CFT of the tubular gastrointestinal tract is very rare with fewer than 30 cases of gastric CFTs reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
